{title: Full of your creatures}
{subtitle: Psalms 104:24}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 90}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Bb] | [F] |
| [C] | [Dm] | [Bb] | [F] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The young [Dm]lions roar for [Bb]their prey
Seeking [F]their food from God a[C]lone
When the [Dm]sun rises in the [Bb]east
They steal a[F]way to lie down in [C]dens
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Instrumental}
| [Dm] | [Bb] | [F] | [C] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Dm]People go out to their [Bb]work
To their [F]labor until evening [C]comes
But the [Dm]earth is full of your crea[Bb]tures
Made [F]by wisdom, one by [C]one
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
How many are your [Dm]works, LORD
[Bb]In wisdom you made them [F]all
The [C]earth is full of your crea[Dm]tures
Great and [Bb]small, standing [F]tall [C]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Dm]There is the sea, vast and [Bb]wide
Teeming with [F]creatures beyond num[C]ber
[Dm]Living things both small and [Bb]great
Ships move a[F]long, that’s the mea[C]sure
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
How many are your [Dm]works, LORD
[Bb]In wisdom you made them [F]all
The [C]earth is full of your crea[Dm]tures
Great and [Bb]small, standing [F][C]tall
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Bb]Leviathan plays in the [Dm]deep
Which you [F]formed to [C]roam
[Bb]All of them look to [Dm]you
To [Bb]give them food [C]in time
{end_of_bridge}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Dm]Look to you for food at [Bb]the proper time
[F]Great are your works, in [C]wisdom made
{end_of_verse}
